# Expectation record for 12_preprocessor/001_macro_expansion_stringize.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 001_macro_expansion_stringize
area               = 12_preprocessor
description        = Function-like and object-like macro expansion, the stringize operator on a token, on an expanded macro and on an expression, token pasting in three forms, nested and self-referential expansion, and a folded/volatile-runtime pair
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour by construction:
- Every printed integer is a small non-negative int far from INT_MIN and INT_MAX, so no
  signed overflow can arise; the largest arithmetic performed is a multiplication whose
  result is well inside int on every target.
- No shift operator appears, so no shift count can be out of range.
- The only pointer arithmetic is walking a string literal to its terminator inside slen,
  which stops AT the terminator: the one-past-end pointer is never formed by
  dereference, and no index beyond the terminator is read. Every string walked is a
  literal in this file, so its length is fixed at translation time.
- No string literal is modified; every literal is read only.
- No aliasing violation and no read of uninitialised storage: every object is
  initialised at its declaration, and the volatile objects have static initialisers.
- No object is modified twice between sequence points, and no argument of any call has a
  side effect, so nothing depends on unspecified evaluation order. Each volatile object
  is read in a statement of its own before its value reaches an argument list.
- Nothing depends on padding bytes or on the relative addresses of unrelated objects.
- The two-variant rule is applied: the same function-like macro is expanded once over a
  literal, where the constant folder answers, and once over an operand read from
  volatile storage, which the optimizer may not fold and which therefore forces the
  backend to emit a genuine multiply. Without the second variant, optimisation would
  substitute the folder's answer for the backend's at -O1 and -O2 and a code-generation
  defect would escape entirely.
- No translation-date, translation-time or source-file-name macro is referenced, there is
  no randomness and no locale-dependent formatting, and main returns 0, inside the 0-125
  range the suite requires.

Verified empirically on this branch with gcc 13.4.0 and qemu-user 10.1.0: the default
strict warning gate (-Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow
-Werror) produces zero diagnostics at -O0, -O1 and -O2; the sanitizer gate
(-fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all) runs to completion with no
output and exit status 0; and all twelve cells of the declared matrix produce
byte-identical stdout with exit status 0 and an empty standard error.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Every construct exercised here is documented as supported - docs/technical-specifications.md
lines 92 and 491 name stringification (#), token pasting (##) and the recursive expansion
guard, and docs/project-guide.md line 79 lists the same - so this program carries no
expected-divergence marker and a divergence under any oracle is a genuine finding.

The measured target differences are handled by construction, so this program needs no
target restriction and no marker:

1. sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) are 4 on i686 and 8 on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64
   (docs/technical-specifications.md lines 457-462). No long, no size_t, no ptrdiff_t
   and no pointer value is printed anywhere, and no length modifier for any of them is
   used, so the difference cannot reach the output.
2. Plain char signedness is implementation-defined and was measured signed on x86_64 and
   i686 and unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64. No plain char value is printed.
3. long double has three representations across the four targets (measured 16, 12, 16 and
   16 bytes, x87 80-bit against IEEE binary128). No long double appears in this program;
   that type is covered by 13_floating_point/004_long_double_target_restricted, which is
   the only program permitted to narrow a comparison on its account.
4. All four targets are little-endian, and no byte-order-sensitive value is printed.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
stringize_direct=WIDTH
stringize_expanded=32
stringize_expression=a + b * 2
stringize_length=5
paste_identifier=55
paste_both_expanded=55
paste_number=12
stringize_of_paste=32
funclike_folded=25
funclike_runtime=16
funclike_nested=14
empty_object_macro=8
self_reference_guard=9
END
